  partName: Clip (2)
  description: The Clip (2) is a small, thin-flat metal component located at the
    middle-center-rear of the engine, used to secure or retain other parts in place.
    Made of mid-tone metal, this clip plays a crucial role in maintaining the engine's
    structural integrity and preventing component misalignment or damage. Notably,
    its small size and rear positioning require precise engineering to ensure reliable
    retention without obstructing nearby components.
